---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Layout/Footer.astro';
import BreadcrumbStructuredData from '../../components/BreadcrumbStructuredData.astro';

const pageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'AsreSEO Privacy Policy',
  url: 'https://asreseo.com/privacy/',
  inLanguage: 'en-US',
};
const breadcrumbs = [
  { position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://asreseo.com/' },
  { position: 2, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: 'https://asreseo.com/privacy/' },
];
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title='Privacy Policy & User Data Protection | AsreSEO' description='AsreSEO privacy policy: how we collect information via contact forms and the newsletter, processing purposes, retention periods, cookies, processors and your rights.' canonical='/privacy/' ogUrl='https://asreseo.com/privacy/' ogType='website' twitterCard='summary_large_image'>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(pageSchema)} />
  <BreadcrumbStructuredData items={breadcrumbs} />
<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#000000] text-slate-100">
            <Header lang="en" />
            <main class="section-padding pt-32">
                <div class="container-custom max-w-4xl">
                    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold mb-8 text-left text-white tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-invert max-w-none text-left text-slate-300" dir="ltr">
                        <p>At AsreSEO, we take your privacy seriously. This page explains what information we collect and through which channels, why we use it, how long we keep it, and how you can exercise your rights as a data subject. This policy applies to the AsreSEO website and the forms and communication channels on it.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">1. Information we collect</h2>
                        <p>When you use our contact form, subscribe to the newsletter, or request a consultation, we receive information such as your name, email address, and message text. Contractual correspondence may also include your business name and address. If providing a service requires limited access to tools such as Search Console or your content management panel, that access is used solely within the scope of that contract and revoked when the engagement ends. When you visit the website, limited technical data such as your IP address, browser type, and visited pages is also recorded automatically and in aggregate.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">2. How we use your information</h2>
                        <p>Your information is used solely to respond to your requests, prepare proposals and enter into contracts, deliver services, send project reports, and — only with your consent — send relevant updates about our services. Newsletter subscription requires your explicit consent, and you can stop receiving it at any time by unsubscribing. We do not sell your contact information, nor do we use it for any purpose beyond those stated on this page.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">3. Retention and deletion</h2>
                        <p>Requests that do not lead to an engagement are kept until that request has been followed up, then deleted or aggregated. Financial and contractual records are kept for as long as the nature of the engagement and legal requirements demand, and deleted afterwards. Newsletter subscription data is retained until you unsubscribe. If you wish, we can also provide you with a copy of the data belonging to you before deletion.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">4. Processors and Automation Infrastructure (n8n)</h2>
                        <p>To deliver our services we use processors such as website hosting, email delivery, traffic analytics tools, and cloud storage. These processors only access data to the extent necessary and are obligated to protect it. Data is shared with them solely for these same purposes. Your information is not shared with any third party outside the scope of these services.</p>
                        <p>Furthermore, automated data pipelines, continuous SEO health monitors, and webhook integrations run on our dedicated workflow automation engine hosted at <a href="https://n8n.asreseo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#CCFF00] font-bold underline hover:no-underline">n8n.asreseo.com</a>. Automated ingestion, model routing, and image payload handling utilize our open-source custom n8n node developments authored by Ali Bakhtiari: <a href="https://github.com/alibakhtiari/n8n-nodes-avvalai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#CCFF00] font-bold underline hover:no-underline">n8n-nodes-avvalai</a> and <a href="https://github.com/alibakhtiari/n8n-nodes-imagerouter" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#CCFF00] font-bold underline hover:no-underline">n8n-nodes-imagerouter</a>. Workflows operating on our self-hosted n8n infrastructure process data in isolated sandboxes with strict zero-trust access controls.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">5. Data security</h2>
                        <p>We use modern security protocols including data-in-transit encryption, internal user access controls, and periodic tool reviews to protect your data. Team members' access to client information is limited to business necessity, and in the event of a security incident involving your data, we will notify you in accordance with legal requirements.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">6. Cookies</h2>
                        <p>This website uses standard cookies to improve your experience. Essential cookies keep the pages' core features working, while analytics cookies show us in aggregate which sections are viewed most. You can block or delete cookies from your browser settings; in that case, some parts of the website may not work correctly.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">7. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
                        <p>You have the right to ask us to provide a copy of the information we hold about you, correct inaccurate or incomplete information, and — where there is no need to retain it or where it was recorded based on your consent — have it deleted. You may also request restriction of processing or object to a specific use of your data.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">8. How to submit your request</h2>
                        <p>To exercise any of the rights above, simply email your request to info@asreseo.com and verify your identity in a way that assures us the data is not disclosed to the wrong person. Your request will be reviewed and the outcome communicated through the same channel. If you do not receive a satisfactory response, you retain the right to appeal to the competent supervisory authorities.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
                        <p>We may update this policy to reflect changes in our services or legal requirements. The current version is always published on this page, and material changes will be announced via email or a notice on the website.</p>

                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">10. Contact us</h2>
                        <p>If you have any questions about this policy or how your personal information is handled, reach us at info@asreseo.com. Our team also answers privacy-related questions before a contract is signed and throughout the engagement.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </main>
            <Footer lang="en" />
        </div>
</BaseLayout>
